            <div type="translation" xml:lang="en" resp="#AA">
                <p>[-] Nonius Flaccus, son of Gaius, of tribe Velina, flamen of the divine Augustus, and the divine Iulius, and the divine Claudius, military tribune 
                    twice of the 5th Macedonian legion and the 7th legion Claudia Pious and Happy, prefect of engineers of Ala I of Pannonia, quinquennial duovir 
                    for the third time, prefect of Imperator Augustus Vespasian, patron of the colony.
                   He ordered this to be made in accordance with his will, at the discretion of Nonia He[---?]. This place was given [by decree of the decurions].
                </p>
            </div>
            <div type="commentary"><!-- Can we work out a date based on which emperors he is flamen of and that he served under Vespasian? -->
                <p></p> 
            </div>
